From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-usb: Register the pipe clock before enabling
 runtime PM

qmp_usb_probe() registers the pipe clock after enabling runtime PM, so
the clock framework enables runtime PM support for it and the clock
takes a runtime PM reference on the PHY device while it is prepared.
The USB pipe clock that the PHY consumes is a child of this clock and
stays prepared from qmp_usb_power_on() to qmp_usb_power_off(). A
powered-on PHY therefore keeps itself runtime active: even when
userspace allows runtime PM through power/control it never runtime
suspends and never enters autonomous mode, so a device plugged into an
idle port cannot wake the controller through the PHY.

Register the pipe clock before runtime PM is enabled. The clock does not
access PHY registers, so it does not need the PHY to be resumed.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
index b0790bcf0bc..d783461d098 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
@@ -2419,6 +2419,17 @@ static int qmp_usb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_node_put;
 
+	/*
+	 * Register the pipe clock before enabling runtime PM. A clock registered
+	 * afterwards takes a runtime PM reference on this device while it is
+	 * prepared, and the pipe clock stays prepared as long as the PHY is
+	 * powered on, so the PHY could never runtime suspend and enter
+	 * autonomous mode. The clock does not touch the PHY registers.
+	 */
+	ret = phy_pipe_clk_register(qmp, np);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_node_put;
+
 	/*
 	 * Enable runtime PM before creating the PHY, phy_create() only enables
 	 * it on the PHY device if already enabled on the parent. Hold a usage
@@ -2435,10 +2446,6 @@ static int qmp_usb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 */
 	pm_runtime_forbid(dev);
 
-	ret = phy_pipe_clk_register(qmp, np);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_pm_put;
-
 	qmp->phy = devm_phy_create(dev, np, &qmp_usb_phy_ops);
 	if (IS_ERR(qmp->phy)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(qmp->phy);
-- 
